EXAMPLE 10 C# Nested If Statement

This program uses nested "if-else" statements to check a person's eligibility.

- It checks whether the person's age is greater than 18.
- If the age is valid, it checks whether the mark is 50 or above.
- If both conditions are true, it displays "You are eligible".
- If the mark is below 50, it displays "You failed".
- If the age is 18 or below, it displays "Age is not allowed".

The program demonstrates how to use nested "if-else" statements to check multiple conditions in C#.








